; rowsum_overflow: a row whose partial sum leaves the i64 range must raise.
;
; linear = [i64::MAX, 1, -1] on a 1x3 grid. The partial sum after the
; second column is 2^63, which is not representable, so ROWSUM raises
; ArithmeticOverflow (SPEC.md's overflow rule on coefficient reductions).
;
; Three columns rather than two, and a third term that brings the exact
; total back inside the range, so the vector discriminates: a wrapping
; implementation pushes i64::MAX -- the exactly correct total -- and
; HALTs. The same program is the only thing pinning the ascending
; flat-index accumulation order ISA.md makes normative, because folding
; the same row in descending order never leaves the range.

PUSH 3
BQMX r0

PUSH 1           ; rows
PUSH 3           ; cols
RESIZE r0

PUSH 0
PUSH 9223372036854775807
SETLINE r0
PUSH 1
PUSH 1
SETLINE r0
PUSH 2
PUSH -1
SETLINE r0

PUSH 0           ; row
ROWSUM r0
HALT
